            <ArticleTitle>Evolution of Radical-Based Convergent Strategies for Total Syntheses of Densely Oxygenated Natural Products.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>460-464</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.accounts.6b00475</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Densely oxygenated natural products often exhibit potent bioactivities and are expected to function as selective cellular probes and novel drug leads. Here we describe our efforts to perfect radical-based convergent strategies for generic total syntheses of these exceedingly challenging structures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
